COPY public.agency_targets (id, year, monthly_retainer_revenue_target, quarterly_project_revenue_target, active_brands_target, avg_client_satisfaction_target, goal_achievement_rate_target, staff_retention_target, set_by, set_at, midyear_reviewed_at, midyear_reviewed_by, notes, created_at, updated_at) FROM stdin;
044df304-cd02-4518-b534-7cec9b73fef4	2027	550000000.00	1000000000.00	50	4.70	85	90	\N	2026-07-25 08:16:27.04061+00	\N	\N	For Monthly Retainer Revenue:\n50 active brands at ~₦11M average. The per-brand rate rises slightly because by 2027 Cerebre has a track record, Sabi data to prove client growth, and pan-African clients who pay premium fees. 12 months = ₦6.6B in retainers alone — already exceeding the entire 2026 target.\n\nFor Quarterly Project Revenue:\nProject revenue doubles because Cerebre is now pitching in Ghana, Kenya, South Africa, and Rwanda — markets where a Nigerian agency with a proven system and African context commands serious fees. Four quarters × ₦1B = ₦4B. Strongest quarters will be Q2 and Q4.\n\nFor Active Brands:\nDouble the 2026 portfolio. At least 10–15 of these 50 brands should be outside Nigeria. The continental footprint is what justifies the "100%+ growth" declaration and positions Cerebre for the 10-country vision in the years beyond 2027.\n\nFor Average Client Satisfaction (4.7 / 5):\nHigher than 2026 because by 2027, Sabi's ClarityScore and real-time task tracking mean problems get fixed before clients even notice them. The system is doing the quality control — the team's job shifts from firefighting to excellence. 4.7 is world-class for a full-service agency at this scale.\n\nFor Goal Achievement Rate:\n5% better than 2026 as internal processes mature. By 2027, Brand Admins have a full year of Sabi data showing exactly which goal types fall behind and why. The improvement comes from smarter goal-setting upstream, not just harder execution downstream.\n\nFor Staff Retention:\t\n90% means Cerebre has become a destination, not a stepping stone. Salaries have risen with revenue, young people are being promoted into leadership on the continent, and the mission is real enough that people stay to see it through. This number also protects the client relationships — the same faces your clients trust are still there.	2026-07-25 08:16:27.04061+00	2026-07-25 08:16:27.04061+00
3726875b-01b1-467e-a574-6db4b396f4db	2026	250000000.00	500000000.00	25	4.50	78	85	\N	2026-07-25 08:10:41.814895+00	2026-07-25 08:10:53.882+00	\N	For Monthly Retainer Revenue:\n25 active brands paying an average of ₦10M/month each. Retainers are the bedrock — they pay salaries, fund operations, and let the team plan. 12 months of this = ₦3B of your ₦5B annual target.\n\nFor Quarterly Project Revenue:\nCampaign builds, brand activations, one-off website or content projects. Four quarters × ₦500M = ₦2B. Added to retainers, that's your ₦5B year. If Q4 is your strongest (typically is), target ₦650M that quarter and use it to fund Q1 2027 hiring.\n\nFor Active Brands:\nAt 25, the portfolio is large enough that losing any one client doesn't break the month, but small enough that every brand still feels like a priority. Mix should be roughly 15 corporate/established brands and 10 growth-stage SMEs.\n\nFor Average Client Satisfaction:\nThis means clients consistently rate their experience as excellent — not just good. On Sabi, every satisfaction score below 4.0 should auto-flag for a Brand Admin check-in. Hitting 4.5 agency-wide in 2026 proves the work is quality, not just promised.\n\nFor Goal Achievement Rate:\t\n4 in every 5 goals set for active brands get completed on time and verified. The 20% gap isn't failure — it's a real-world buffer for scope changes and client delays. Below 70% means the goal-setting process needs tightening, not just the execution.\n\nFor Staff Retention:\n8 out of every 10 people who started the year are still here at year-end. This is healthy: high enough to preserve institutional knowledge, low enough that the team stays dynamic. Anything below 75% in 2026 should trigger a compensation and culture audit immediately.	2026-07-25 08:10:41.814895+00	2026-08-06 10:55:29.969+00
\.
